  "issue_number": 3489,
  "issue_title": "Add a raw pallet-event-mix panel using the Postgres all-events stats endpoint",
  "issue_body": "## Context\n\n`GET /api/v1/chain-events/stats` returns the pallet.method event-distribution aggregate over the Postgres all-events tier (ADR 0013) \u2014 distinct from the D1-backed `/api/v1/chain/activity` and `/api/v1/chain/calls` the UI already consumes. Those two D1 aggregates are rendered today in `apps/ui/src/routes/explorer.tsx` (`chainActivityQuery` \u2192 daily activity series, `chainCallsQuery` \u2192 the `CallMixSection` call-mix panel), but nothing in the frontend calls the raw all-events stats endpoint \u2014 it is backend-only right now, reachable only via the `get_chain_activity` MCP tool.\n\n## Requirement\n\nAdd a raw pallet-event-mix panel to the chain explorer dashboard that renders the `pallet.method` event distribution from `GET /api/v1/chain-events/stats`, positioned as the raw-tier sibling of the existing curated `CallMixSection`.\n\n## Backend\n\n- Endpoint: `GET /api/v1/chain-events/stats` (`src/contracts.mjs:2784-2799`) \u2014 accepts `?blocks` (default 1000, capped 5000); returns `{ window_blocks, groups, activity: [...] }` where `groups` is the distinct pallet.method count and `activity` is ordered by `count` descending (top 100), each row shaped `{ pallet, method, count }` (confirmed via `loadChainActivity` in `src/mcp-server.mjs:965-975` and the `get_chain_activity` tool description at `src/mcp-server.mjs:5522-5530`: \"the pallet.method event distribution (each with its count, busiest first)\"). Served live, no static artifact; empty (`groups: 0, activity: []`) before the all-events backfill runs.\n- Query function: **none exists.** A full grep of `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/queries.ts` (5044 lines) turns up no function calling `/api/v1/chain-events/stats` \u2014 only the D1-backed `chainActivityQuery` (line 2297, \u2192 `/api/v1/chain/activity`) and `chainCallsQuery` (line 2321, \u2192 `/api/v1/chain/calls`). `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/types.ts` likewise has no matching type (checked around `ChainActivity`/`ChainCalls` at lines 1573-1594 \u2014 nothing for chain-events-stats). This PR must add the typed query function AS WELL AS the UI wiring in one PR: a new `chainEventsStatsQuery(blocks)` in `queries.ts` following the exact `queryOptions` + `apiFetch` + `isRecord`/`firstFiniteNumber` normalize pattern used by `chainCallsQuery` (lines 2321-2345) and its `normalizeChainRows`/`normalizeChainCallEntry` helpers (lines 2208, 2285-2295), plus a matching `ChainEventsStats`/`ChainEventsStatsEntry` interface pair in `types.ts` mirroring the `ChainCalls`/`ChainCallEntry` shape at lines 1580-1594.\n\n## Deliverable\n\n- File(s) to change: `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/queries.ts` (new `chainEventsStatsQuery`), `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/types.ts` (new `ChainEventsStats`/`ChainEventsStatsEntry`), and `apps/ui/src/routes/explorer.tsx` \u2014 confirmed this route exists and is exactly the dashboard already rendering the two aggregates this endpoint is \"distinct from.\"\n- Exact anchor: `explorer.tsx` already defines `CallMixSection` (lines 137-223, using `ChainCalls` from `@/lib/metagraphed/types`) and renders it at line 456 inside `<div className=\"grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2\">` next to \"Most active accounts\" (lines 454-474+). Add a new `PalletEventMixSection` component in the same file, following the identical `rounded-lg border border-border bg-card p-5` section shell and header pattern used throughout the file (e.g. lines 147-155, 304-310), and fetch it in `ExplorerDashboard` (line 225+) alongside the existing `useSuspenseQuery(chainActivityQuery(win))` / `useSuspenseQuery(chainCallsQuery(win))` calls (lines 230-233). Also append `/api/v1/chain-events/stats` to the `ApiSourceFooter` `paths` array at lines 77-84 (currently lists only the four `/api/v1/chain/*` paths).\n- What to render: reuse the same leaderboard-list idiom `CallMixSection` already uses \u2014 a ranked `<ul>` of top pallet.method rows with a proportional bar (`relative h-1.5 ... rounded-full` fill scaled to the max count in view, matching lines 158-196) rather than introducing a new chart primitive, since this panel is the raw-tier counterpart to that exact section. Populate from `activity` (each row's `pallet`, `method`, `count`), a header showing `groups` distinct pallet.method pairs and the `window_blocks` used, and cap the rendered rows the same way `CallMixSection` caps `modules` to 10 (line 138).\n- Coordination note: this is the twin of the existing `CallMixSection` (`chainCallsQuery` \u2192 D1 `/api/v1/chain/calls`) in the same file \u2014 a reviewer should expect this PR to add a new section near, but not replace, `CallMixSection`. It is filed in the same \"Block-explorer aggregates + perf\" batch as #3488 (block-production stats header, `blocks.index.tsx`) and #3490 (search-index swap for the omnibox) \u2014 those touch different files and are independent.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Diff touches at least one file under `apps/ui/src/routes/` or `apps/ui/src/components/` (not just `queries.ts`/`types.ts`)\n- [ ] `apps/ui/src/routes/explorer.tsx` imports and calls the new `chainEventsStatsQuery` via `useSuspenseQuery` (matching the file's existing `useSuspenseQuery(chainActivityQuery(win))` / `useSuspenseQuery(chainCallsQuery(win))` convention, not a bare `useQuery`)\n- [ ] The rendered panel shows, per row, the `pallet`, `method`, and `count` from the `activity` array, ranked by count descending, plus a `groups` (distinct pallet.method pairs) summary figure\n- [ ] `/api/v1/chain-events/stats` is added to the `ApiSourceFooter` `paths` list in `explorer.tsx`\n- [ ] Loading + empty + error states match the file's existing convention: `Suspense`/`QueryErrorBoundary` at the page level (lines 72-76) for loading/error, and an inline \"No \u2026 yet\" `<p className=\"font-mono text-[12px] text-ink-muted\">` fallback for the empty-array case, mirroring `CallMixSection`'s own empty branch (line 219) and the \"No activity indexed yet\" copy (lines 349-352)\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- Do not touch `CallMixSection` itself or its underlying `chainCallsQuery`/`/api/v1/chain/calls` D1 aggregate \u2014 that panel stays as-is; this issue only adds the new raw-tier panel alongside it.\n- Do not touch `blocks.index.tsx` (that's #3488's block-production stats header) or the omnibox/command-palette search wiring (that's #3490) \u2014 both are separate issues in the same tracker batch.\n- Do not add a `?blocks` window-size selector UI control in this PR unless trivially reusing the existing `win`/window-toggle state; a dedicated blocks-window picker is out of scope here.\n\n## Size\n\nSize: S \u2014 keep this PR small (aim for \u226410 files / \u22641000 LOC).\n\nPart of #2542.",
